cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software, please cite both the software and the paper below.
type: software
title: "stabilitygate: a three-outcome test-retest stability screen for repeated-call LLM experiments"
abstract: >-
  A correlation-based test-retest gate becomes uninformative, and at saturated
  baselines inverted, when matched cells hold too little reliable between-cell
  variance for a correlation to read. stabilitygate replaces that gate with a
  screen returning one of three verdicts, no_drift_detected, FAIL or
  INDETERMINATE, together with a design-time calibration routine that reports the
  operating characteristics of a planned design before any data are collected.
  The admitting verdict is a failure to reject a no-drift null rather than a
  rejection of consequential drift, and the package is not an equivalence test.
  Its measured operating characteristics are scoped by name to the configuration
  stabilitygate.presets.OC_2026_08_28 and are reported in full in the README.
